			   README file for

			    ptouch-driver

This is ptouch-driver, a printer driver based on CUPS and foomatic,
for the Brother P-touch and QL label printer families.

ptouch-driver was originally developed by Arne John Glenstrup.  Maintenance has
(as of September 2015) been taken over by Phil Pemberton.

A significant code clean-up was done by Andreas Gruenbacher in May 2020.

See the file `INSTALL' for directions on how to install this software.

After installing, you will probably have to reload or restart CUPS.

This package contains the following directories:

  .        raster filter (rastertoptouch.c)
  driver   foomatic driver XML files
  opt      foomatic options XML files
  printer  foomatic printer XML files

Page rotation
-------------

PT printers offer RotatePage=None (the default), CW, and CCW. CW rotates
clockwise and CCW counterclockwise, as viewed on the printed page. The
option exchanges physical paper width and height while preserving the
original logical page size seen by PostScript document code. Rasterization
uses the printer's selected horizontal and vertical resolutions.

Use this for documents whose width must run along the tape. Leave it off
when the application already rotates its output, and avoid combining it
with a separate CUPS landscape/orientation override. Other printer settings
and QL printers are unchanged.

Rendering controls
------------------

PT printers offer the following additional options:

  DitherMode       Screen (default) or ErrorDiffusion
  ScreenFrequency  Ghostscript default, or 20/30/45/60/75/85 lpi
  ScreenAngle      Ghostscript default, or 0/15/30/45/60/75/90 degrees
  MinFeatureSize   1 (default) or 2; error diffusion only
  ToneGamma        0.70/0.85/1.0/1.2/1.4/1.8/2.2
  ToneBrightness   -20/-10/0/+10/+20/+30 percent
  ToneContrast     50/75/100/125/150/200 percent

Screen frequency and angle apply to Screen mode. Tone controls apply before
rasterization, in the order gamma, contrast, brightness, then clipping.
Gamma above 1 lightens midtones while preserving black and white; additive
brightness can turn black text gray. Non-neutral tone settings replace
PostScript document transfer functions, including per-page resets. Neutral
settings preserve the document's transfer functions.

Foomatic invokes Ghostscript with cups output in Screen mode or pngmonod
in ErrorDiffusion mode. The installed ptouch-raster-bridge passes native
CUPS raster unchanged, or converts consecutive 1-bit monochrome PNG pages
to CUPS raster. Ghostscript performs the dithering; rastertoptch continues
to generate the Brother protocol. QL rendering is unchanged.

Building requires the CUPS and libpng development files, a C compiler,
make, Autoconf, Automake, Perl, and XML::LibXML. The filter programs install
under ${libdir}/cups/filter and the prepared XML files under
${datadir}/foomatic/db/source. Match those locations to the CUPS and
Foomatic installation in use; their search paths do not change with this
package's prefix. Foomatic generates PPDs from the installed XML database.
Existing queues retain their copied PPDs until explicitly updated.

PT-P950NW defaults
------------------

The PT-P950NW defaults to MirrorPrint=False, RotatePage=CCW,
DitherMode=ErrorDiffusion, and ToneGamma=G140. Other PT models retain
Screen mode, no rotation, and neutral tone settings. Per-user printer
options can override both queue defaults and settings remembered by GTK
applications; remove redundant user overrides if dialog choices reset.

Offline printing tests
----------------------

Run make check after building to exercise the filters without printing or
changing the system database. These tests additionally require Python 3,
Ghostscript, cupsfilter, cupstestppd, and foomatic-ppdfile (Debian/Devuan:
python3, ghostscript, cups, cups-client, cups-filters, foomatic-db-engine).
No additional Python packages are needed. Set FOOMATIC_PPDFILE in the
environment to use a different foomatic-ppdfile executable.

The tests generate their PPDs from a temporary database of the prepared
build XML. They cover PPD syntax and defaults, malformed/multi-page input,
tone controls, raster settings, page changes, rotation and pixel polarity.
These checks do not replace physical printing on the supported models.
To compare output against PPDs from an earlier source revision, run:

  python3 ../tests/check-printing.py --builddir . \
      --baseline-ppds /path/to/old/ppds --keep "$PWD/check-results"

Please note: This software is not in any way related to Brother
Industries, Ltd., except that it is intended for use with their
products.  Any comments to this software should NOT be directed to
Brother Industries, Ltd.

